    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Luis Arraez** (66.44) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.31) anchor our lineup, benefiting immensely from a favorable matchup against Miles Mikolas. Mikolas presents a high xERA of 4.62, and with wind conditions blowing out at the park, both **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee**\u2014along with **Matt Chapman** (64.11)\u2014see a significant boost to their efficiency scores. **Taylor Ward** (60.43) also clears the 60-point threshold despite a neutral matchup, as his spot at the top of the order provides the volume necessary to remain a high-floor play. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (62.93) remains an auto-start; while he faces a tougher arm in Will Warren, his elite batting order placement keeps his score firmly in the strong category.\n\nThe most difficult sit-start decision involved **Lawrence Butler**, who fell just short of the cut at 39.10. While his base projection is solid, the optimizer penalized him for a sub-optimal matchup against Kyle Harrison (3.32 xERA) and the significant dynamic platoon disadvantage created by the left-on-left tilt. Consequently, we are prioritizing players like **Drew Gilbert** and **Jeremiah Jackson**\u2014despite their lower lineup positions\u2014because the park factors and weaker opposing starters provide a better projected path to production than the risk associated with **Lawrence Butler** or **Jonathan Aranda** today.\n\nWe are operating with a heavy \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board, which introduces non-zero risk to our efficiency targets. **Daulton Varsho** (40.69) is the most precarious start in the outfield; he faces an elite arm in Cristopher S\u00e1nchez (2.74 xERA), and his score is depressed by both a platoon disadvantage and the negative impact of his catcher-profile drag on his total offensive output. Should the official lineups reveal unexpected shifts, we may need to reconsider the utilization of bench depth, keeping in mind that **Cal Raleigh** remains sidelined on the IL and **Will Smith** is unavailable due to a team off-day. Proceed with caution on **Daulton Varsho**; if his position in the order drops further, he risks falling below our functional floor.",
